  "term": "neuroleptic malignant syndrome",
  "definition": "Neuroleptic malignant syndrome is a rare but potentially fatal reaction linked mainly to neuroleptic (antipsychotic) drugs. It involves severe muscle rigidity, tremor, high fever, sweating, unstable blood pressure, thinking changes, and other autonomic disturbances.",
